  "body": "Part of #2607 (slice S6 of 6).\n\nThe order of the maintainer (2026-11-18): \"GPU shader issues get priority\".\n\n## What\n- Move `crates/ui/src/trace.rs`, `trace.wgsl` and the eye code that they need into `camcraft-gpu` (#2620). Then simview can draw without `camcraft-ui` or flecs.\n- simview (#2587) uses the GPU playback of S3 (#2629).\n- Browser: WebGPU uses the GPU path. The display needs no read-back, so no blocking wait is necessary. WebGL2 has no compute (`DownlevelFlags::COMPUTE_SHADERS`) and uses the CPU path. The browser probe is #2623.\n\n## Decision entry\nA `docs/decisions/` entry for the `simview -> camcraft-gpu` edge is necessary (AGENTS.md \"No new dependency between our crates without a decision\").\n\n## Tests\n- `crates/ui/tests/trace_parity.rs` moves with the code and stays green. The `#[test]` count does not go down.\n- A simview headless test plays a program on the software adapter and on the CPU path.\n\nBlocked by #2629 (S3) and #2587 (the simview window).\n\nDone means: the trace lives in `camcraft-gpu`, simview plays on the GPU, the browser uses WebGPU or the CPU path, and the tests are green.\n",
